1769712724211952	bob	itc:v3:AWKSc8kyZJPJk5EAAAAAQau9WtV610AAAAEzAQ		item.create	bn-b8c50263d	{"description":"Reduce round-trips for complex interaction sequences.\n\nUsage:\n  botty script <agent-id> <<EOF\ntest-edge\n:sleep 500\n:enter\n:sleep 500\n:key down\n:snapshot\nEOF\n\nOr JSON/YAML format for programmatic generation.\n\nCurrently need separate botty send/sleep/send calls, which is slow and verbose for long sequences.\n\n## Triage Notes (2026-01-29)\n**Complexity**: Medium-High - new command, parser, format design, error handling\n**Concerns**: Overlap with record/replay (bd-2lj), unproven need (is round-trip latency really a problem?)\n**Value**: Reduces latency but unclear if this is actually painful\n**Implementation**: ~6-10 hours\n**Downgrade**: P3→P4 - Wait for user feedback showing round-trip latency causes real pain. May be superseded by bd-2lj.\n\nImported beads fields:\nclose_reason:\nClosing as won't implement. This overlaps significantly with bd-2lj (record/replay). If we implement record/replay, it would generate scripts that could be replayed. If round-trip latency becomes a proven issue, the right solution is protocol-level request batching, not a script DSL. Adds API surface without demonstrated need. Will reconsider if users report round-trip latency as a real pain point.\n\ncompaction_level:\n0\n\ncontent_hash:\n87240d043092748877f3694d6affbe2b9d045b33ccb2aed2769bb1d6e56645ad\n\nephemeral:\n0\n\nis_template:\n0\n\noriginal_size:\n0\n\npinned:\n0\n\nsource_repo:\n.","kind":"task","title":"Add multi-step send with timing (script mode)"}	blake3:6VBo3yLQlcokKR9MZkbwArrEovAO_kRcAC3nYd7KTAM
