1769782166383788	bob	itc:v3:AWKSc8kyZJPJk5EAAAAAQau9WtV610AAAAEzCQ		item.create	bn-b2adaf33c	{"description":"Implement a tmux command palette for the 'botty view' session, accessible via a keybinding (e.g., Ctrl+P). This palette should offer quick access to common botty actions within the active tmux session.\n\n**Actions to include:**\n- Shutdown Botty server (`botty shutdown`)\n- Detach from the current botty tmux session (`detach-client`)\n- Refresh/re-layout botty panes (if such a command exists or can be simulated with `tmux refresh-client -S`)\n- List currently active agents (`botty list`)\n- Potentially a 'Help' entry\n\n**Implementation details:**\n- Use `tmux display-menu` to create the interactive menu.\n- Bind the menu to a key in the botty-managed tmux session configuration.\n- Actions should trigger relevant `botty` CLI commands or native tmux commands.\n- Consider context (e.g., if the botty server isn't running, 'shutdown' should be disabled or lead to a 'server not running' message).\n\nImported beads fields:\nclose_reason:\nImplemented in 7a6561d5. Ctrl+P opens tmux display-menu with List Agents, Snapshot Pane, Refresh Layout, Detach, and Shutdown.\n\ncompaction_level:\n0\n\ncontent_hash:\n2c276dc51cbea3d08ba92c41efe7d28b344eed7d8355be962bb41461a48a84e1\n\nephemeral:\n0\n\nis_template:\n0\n\noriginal_size:\n0\n\npinned:\n0\n\nsource_repo:\n.","kind":"task","title":"Add tmux command palette to botty view"}	blake3:MB1CQd6ILfQAioGORfMe6EGtl0zhIWXX-BKxTmDrwmQ
