1769798865999845	bob	itc:v3:AWKSc8kyZJPJk5EAAAAAQau9WtV610AAAAEzDQ		item.create	bn-bad6053ff	{"description":"Intermittent issue: After detaching from botty view and using --new-session, sometimes see this warning:\n\n2026-01-30T18:18:19.545788Z  WARN botty::server: Attach session error: I/O error: Broken pipe (os error 32)\n\nThe second time running view --new-session, the error doesn't appear and htop looks fine.\n\n## Investigation needed:\n- [ ] Reproduce consistently\n- [ ] Determine if this is a race condition in view detach/reattach\n- [ ] Check if this is related to bd-6jk (view cleanup on detach)\n- [ ] Verify if it actually breaks functionality or just logs a warning\n\n## Acceptance criteria:\n- [ ] Understand root cause\n- [ ] Determine if this is actually a bug or just noisy logging\n- [ ] Fix if it breaks functionality, or suppress warning if benign\n\nImported beads fields:\nclose_reason:\nFixed in commit 59175309. Root cause identified: tmux kill-session abruptly terminates attach processes, causing expected broken pipe errors. Fixed by downgrading broken pipe warnings to debug level. No functional issue - htop and other TUI programs work fine. Investigation documented in commit message.\n\ncompaction_level:\n0\n\ncontent_hash:\n495bafa62eb4044ed5bdfa017ae8448b21227f92640cf3441ba08cb8bb4f3538\n\nephemeral:\n0\n\nis_template:\n0\n\noriginal_size:\n0\n\npinned:\n0\n\nsource_repo:\n.","kind":"bug","title":"view --new-session logs warning, messes up htop"}	blake3:s6htmQyHxGKoVZ0ws7i1K2wk6-y7O5L1cehRNiYyoLQ
