1771184023576153	botty-dev	itc:v3:AWLnk5P-ZJJJxAAAAAAAQe9df9qquAAAAAEuAw		item.create	bn-bac4582a0	{"description":"The reattach path in run_view_command (src/main.rs:2002) skips create_session() and never re-sets remain-on-exit on the window. If the session was created by an older botty version or the option got cleared, the last pane process exiting destroys the session. Fix: in the reattach path, ensure remain-on-exit is set on the agents window, same as create_session does.\n\nImported beads fields:\nclose_reason:\nFixed in v0.13.0. Reattach path now calls ensure_remain_on_exit().\n\ncompaction_level:\n0\n\ncontent_hash:\n4a2f0305a2c6ff39f5b4545be9193aeb63bb8ab47c0c8e85b1a2bd074594e60b\n\nephemeral:\n0\n\nis_template:\n0\n\noriginal_size:\n0\n\nowner:\nbotty-dev\n\npinned:\n0\n\nsource_repo:\n.","kind":"bug","title":"view reattach: ensure remain-on-exit is set"}	blake3:VUlZQLqjDDIbTwX0Nk7nKmVeREjo7MmqmvGwaE6xHgg
1771208440783303	botty-dev	itc:v3:AWLnk5P-ZJJJxAAAAAAAQe9df9qquAAAAAEuBA	blake3:VUlZQLqjDDIbTwX0Nk7nKmVeREjo7MmqmvGwaE6xHgg	item.move	bn-bac4582a0	{"reason":"Imported from beads","state":"done"}	blake3:WKyIr_5syFKMQ_lkbCuEVLVB4ie2QKq_F6UC94BMGq0
1769543517100877	bob	itc:v3:AWKSc8kyZJPJk5EAAAAAQau9WtV610AAAAEzGw		item.create	bn-b618f459a	{"description":"The tool was built for spawning agents, but it's really a PTY manager that could be used for anything (TUI development, terminal multiplexing, screen capture).\n\nCurrent naming ('agent') is confusing when spawning non-agent programs like htop.\n\nOptions:\n- `pty` - technically accurate, jargon-y\n- `session` - tmux-like, generic\n- `terminal` / `term` - user-friendly\n\nWould affect:\n- CLI output ('agents' → 'sessions' or 'ptys')\n- Protocol: SpawnAgent → Spawn, AgentId → SessionId/PtyId\n- Code: struct Agent → struct Session/Pty\n- Docs, error messages, help text\n\nNote: The name 'botty' itself implies bots/agents but could just be quirky branding.\n\nImported beads fields:\nclose_reason:\nDeferred: Large refactor affecting entire codebase (CLI, protocol, code, docs). Current naming 'agent' is acceptable and consistent. Not worth the churn unless project scope expands significantly. Would revisit if botty becomes a general-purpose terminal multiplexer.\n\ncompaction_level:\n0\n\ncontent_hash:\n967ac3b31dc2527223af00689f6f5b430cd01c9d6ffb9cea2cb0b93356a11f0d\n\nephemeral:\n0\n\nis_template:\n0\n\noriginal_size:\n0\n\npinned:\n0\n\nsource_repo:\n.","kind":"task","title":"Consider renaming 'agent' to 'pty' or 'session' in data model"}	blake3:0gKeLfBzzfDmD5RpvByGDeEbp4pToanMZPME7m3g-zs
1769874465559934	bob	itc:v3:AWKSc8kyZJPJk5EAAAAAQau9WtV610AAAAEzHA	blake3:0gKeLfBzzfDmD5RpvByGDeEbp4pToanMZPME7m3g-zs	item.move	bn-b618f459a	{"reason":"Imported from beads","state":"done"}	blake3:zMXvz1PBqp7If38laMkHzMKy00tB6sWunSfrYr4wPcA
1770070864631479	bob	itc:v3:AWKSc8kyZJPJk5EAAAAAQau9WtV610AAAAEzHQ		item.create	bn-b537c5b0f	{"description":"Add a --no-resize flag to botty spawn that marks an agent as resize-immune. When view's auto-resize runs (resize_agents_to_panes), it skips agents with this flag. This prevents view from corrupting snapshot dimensions for agents that scripts/other processes are reading programmatically.\n\nImplementation:\n- Add no_resize: bool to Agent struct\n- Add --no-resize to spawn CLI and Request::Spawn protocol\n- Pass through server handler to Agent::new\n- In resize_agents_to_panes (main.rs ~2071), skip agents where no_resize is true\n- Include no_resize in AgentInfo so list output shows it\n\nAcceptance criteria:\n- [ ] botty spawn --no-resize -- bash starts agent with resize lock\n- [ ] botty view auto-resize skips no-resize agents\n- [ ] botty resize <id> still works (explicit resize is allowed)\n- [ ] botty list shows no-resize status\n- [ ] All existing tests pass\n\nImported beads fields:\nclose_reason:\nImplemented --no-resize flag on spawn. Agents with this flag are skipped by view's auto-resize (both initial and tmux hook paths). Explicit botty resize still works. Flag shown in list JSON output.\n\ncompaction_level:\n0\n\ncontent_hash:\n36990ae2d464fcb9145bf02a5e13b9cf7eb255c33a633beb0f659499426aa35a\n\nephemeral:\n0\n\nis_template:\n0\n\noriginal_size:\n0\n\npinned:\n0\n\nsource_repo:\n.","kind":"task","title":"Add --no-resize flag to spawn command"}	blake3:AAeZML3gOKppdd6l4VeeX-EQaDzhw7CdhTSihhdUV0o
1770076420066124	bob	itc:v3:AWKSc8kyZJPJk5EAAAAAQau9WtV610AAAAEzHg	blake3:AAeZML3gOKppdd6l4VeeX-EQaDzhw7CdhTSihhdUV0o	item.move	bn-b537c5b0f	{"reason":"Imported from beads","state":"done"}	blake3:8XPe3w66FmA4yTtAo1_FF4CWn20NYVPPB-Z1x9g8uU4
1771478157851553	1	itc:v3:AWKTMnkmSTJyZnQAAAAAQa2vVqtdbcAAAAEyAQ		item.create	bn-b696772a0	{"description":"Add an ergonomic shorthand to `botty send` for submitting Enter without requiring a separate `send-keys` call.\n\nProblem:\nIn PTY automation flows, callers often send prompt text and then need to trigger Enter as a second command (`botty send-keys <id> enter`). This adds friction and can create ambiguity around submission semantics.\n\nRequested behavior:\n- Support `botty send <id> \"text\" --enter` as shorthand for appending an Enter key submission to the send operation.\n- `--enter` should be equivalent to current newline submit behavior expected by users, but explicitly modeled as Enter keypress semantics.\n- Keep existing `--newline` behavior backward-compatible.\n\nAcceptance criteria:\n- `botty send --enter` is documented in help.\n- Works with and without text payload (e.g., empty send that just presses Enter).\n- Covered by tests.\n- No regression to existing `--newline` or `send-keys enter` workflows.\n\nImported beads fields:\nclose_reason:\nImplemented --enter/-e flag on send command. Appends CR (0x0d) matching send-keys enter semantics. Text optional with --enter.\n\ncompaction_level:\n0\n\ncontent_hash:\n87908c7924d78134ce9038b367d23815ac246600ed7b9cde368315dea39cfa27\n\nephemeral:\n0\n\nis_template:\n0\n\noriginal_size:\n0\n\nowner:\nbotty-dev\n\npinned:\n0\n\nsource_repo:\n.","kind":"task","title":"Add send --enter shorthand to submit Enter key"}	blake3:1XySk-CVRPSXoYKUmsGz-cRSmnZWDCdpFqHkpGhplJs
1771533846798608	1	itc:v3:AWKTMnkmSTJyZnQAAAAAQa2vVqtdbcAAAAEyAg	blake3:1XySk-CVRPSXoYKUmsGz-cRSmnZWDCdpFqHkpGhplJs	item.move	bn-b696772a0	{"reason":"Imported from beads","state":"done"}	blake3:M6gg4xmTohs7FUb2h4lMyD5gZ6BF-IMkCgjn7r9VLe0
1771191598969397	botty-dev	itc:v3:AWLnk5P-ZJJJxAAAAAAAQe9df9qquAAAAAEuBQ		item.create	bn-b568c9d9e	{"description":"Change wait command to accept multiple agent IDs (id: Vec<String>) so you can do 'botty wait --exited agent1 agent2 agent3'. Subscribe to events for all specified agents, track which have exited, break when all are done. Exit code: highest non-zero from any agent. Only allow multiple IDs with --exited; error if combined with screen-based conditions (--contains, --pattern, --stable) since those are inherently single-agent. Single-ID usage stays unchanged.\n\nImported beads fields:\nclose_reason:\nImplemented in v0.13.0. wait --exited now accepts multiple agent IDs.\n\ncompaction_level:\n0\n\ncontent_hash:\n77d41eb9adec3491e110d5fc9a6395e42885a22b985ebf8093bfdc5882399929\n\nephemeral:\n0\n\nis_template:\n0\n\noriginal_size:\n0\n\nowner:\nbotty-dev\n\npinned:\n0\n\nsource_repo:\n.","kind":"task","title":"wait --exited: support multiple agent IDs"}	blake3:YyWQc-p-gHXEyB1MMV-fpM4s9Yc3S3Gkhlgdzy-q1uw
