1769890562412850	bob	itc:v3:AWKSc8kyZJPJk5EAAAAAQau9WtV610AAAAEzIw		item.create	bn-bae869bc4	{"description":"When running botty view --new-session after spawning htop, the UI is broken with missing elements.\n\nReproduction:\n1. botty view\n2. botty spawn -- htop\n3. botty view --new-session\n4. Result: htop UI has missing elements all over the place\n\nThis might be related to:\n- How --new-session kills and recreates the tmux session\n- The broken pipe fix we just made (bd-1ax)\n- Screen/terminal state not being properly reset\n- PTY state corruption when panes are forcibly killed\n\nNeed to investigate what's happening to the htop agent's PTY when the tmux session is killed and recreated.\n\nImported beads fields:\nclose_reason:\nFixed in commit 6d402b31. Root cause: attach didn't send initial resize, only on SIGWINCH. When view --new-session recreated panes at different sizes, PTYs were out of sync with terminals, causing garbled TUI rendering. Fix: send initial resize request to sync PTY with terminal dimensions on attach start.\n\ncompaction_level:\n0\n\ncontent_hash:\neb3bd1f0ebd47792710ce37f4829e86ddce90ef16510376dcef8de02a744e781\n\nephemeral:\n0\n\nis_template:\n0\n\noriginal_size:\n0\n\npinned:\n0\n\nsource_repo:\n.","kind":"bug","labels":["punt"],"title":"view --new-session breaks htop UI"}	blake3:hyV82IrgvyDCuktjkdPk1nPnCLk5hjnqQMdNxHKGRkM
1769893421000000	Bob	itc:v3:AWLMkySZyc5nk0AAAAAAQdq1W67t6wAAAAEwAQ	blake3:hyV82IrgvyDCuktjkdPk1nPnCLk5hjnqQMdNxHKGRkM	item.comment	bn-bae869bc4	{"body":"User deprioritized 2026-01-31: Multiple fix attempts (SIGWINCH on clear, skip stale screen render) didn't resolve the issue reliably. Leaving open but deprioritized for now."}	blake3:o9TcOl389O5yYcsjxBswOZxC7Yaq7dQmrw_pCr0mqx0
1769557943373762	bob	itc:v3:AWKSc8kyZJPJk5EAAAAAQau9WtV610AAAAEzJA		item.create	bn-b9cd0d1fd	{"description":"Allow multiple botty view instances to run simultaneously without interfering.\n\n## Problem\nThe tmux session name is hardcoded as 'botty', which means:\n- Can't run multiple view instances\n- Multiple users on same machine would conflict\n- Reattaching might grab wrong session\n\n## Proposed solutions\n1. Generate unique session names (e.g., 'botty-<pid>' or 'botty-<uuid>')\n2. Add --session flag to specify custom name\n3. Both: generate by default, allow override\n\n## Implementation notes\nFrom security review cr-klwd (th-grfz). Low security impact, mainly a usability issue.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] Multiple `botty view` instances can run simultaneously\n- [ ] Each gets unique tmux session name\n- [ ] Session names are discoverable (maybe `botty view --list`?)\n- [ ] Can specify custom session name with `--session`\n- [ ] Default naming is predictable (e.g., botty-<pid>)\n\n## Labels\nview, tmux, enhancement\n\nImported beads fields:\ncompaction_level:\n0\n\ncontent_hash:\n20e96c411ece4a02c7ea8e0c6509a920169a2ff77340127b023dbf9311396535\n\nephemeral:\n0\n\nis_template:\n0\n\noriginal_size:\n0\n\npinned:\n0\n\nsource_repo:\n.","kind":"task","labels":["punt"],"title":"Support unique tmux session names per view instance"}	blake3:5OTgE9kX_iWTSlplmmjuSneyN9vj-o6mSASrRGBqRXc
1769295360130881	bob	itc:v3:AWKSc8kyZJPJk5EAAAAAQau9WtV610AAAAEzJQ		item.create	bn-b0f150d2d	{"description":"Create server module with tokio-based Unix socket listener, handle incoming connections, dispatch to request handlers. Include auto-fork/daemonize logic.\n\nImported beads fields:\nclose_reason:\nImplemented server with Unix socket listener, request handling, PTY output polling\n\ncompaction_level:\n0\n\ncontent_hash:\n622f246cabb344278fb32afd0895cc66259c878909b8d57e1352c4acce3beeb6\n\nephemeral:\n0\n\nis_template:\n0\n\noriginal_size:\n0\n\npinned:\n0\n\nsource_repo:\n.","kind":"task","title":"Server skeleton with Unix socket listener"}	blake3:gJg3AR404Z30377xLHOU5dbV9FsQxhBXQLmIx3SjSK4
