1770503519869272	botty-dev	itc:v3:AWLnk5P-ZJJJxAAAAAAAQe9df9qquAAAAAEuBw		item.create	bn-bb1c855c4	{"description":"When `botty shutdown` is run, it stops the server but leaves the tmux session (\"botty\") running. The tmux session should be killed as part of shutdown to avoid orphaned sessions.\n\nNote: The detach handler (main.rs:1789-1798) already does this when no agents are running after detach. The shutdown command should do the same unconditionally.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] `botty shutdown` kills the tmux session in addition to stopping the server\n- [ ] Works even if agents are still running (shutdown is intentional teardown)\n- [ ] No error if tmux session does not exist (idempotent)\n\n## Testing\n- `botty view && botty spawn -- bash && botty shutdown` — verify no orphaned tmux session\n- `botty shutdown` without view running — should not error\n- Check `tmux ls` after shutdown confirms session is gone\n\nImported beads fields:\nclose_reason:\nMerged. Shutdown now kills tmux session.\n\ncompaction_level:\n0\n\ncontent_hash:\nc7547f4a0bd49ce94759b4fe1371c09f6cc89572ab0fd28a94863e48861da7c7\n\nephemeral:\n0\n\nis_template:\n0\n\noriginal_size:\n0\n\nowner:\nbotty-dev\n\npinned:\n0\n\nsource_repo:\n.","kind":"task","title":"shutdown should kill the botty tmux session"}	blake3:qjmSwaeHYGg_r26zL6mYBw8FzgwE9Z4sVaovHD8rLNA
1770645495469989	botty-dev	itc:v3:AWLnk5P-ZJJJxAAAAAAAQe9df9qquAAAAAEuCA	blake3:qjmSwaeHYGg_r26zL6mYBw8FzgwE9Z4sVaovHD8rLNA	item.move	bn-bb1c855c4	{"reason":"Imported from beads","state":"done"}	blake3:ZgXJX6k-onhNbQVRriwmefsEEDjdCQyvP3_dCKFurd0
0	botty-dev	itc:v3:AWLnk5P-ZJJJxAAAAAAAQe9df9qquAAAAAEuCQ	blake3:ZgXJX6k-onhNbQVRriwmefsEEDjdCQyvP3_dCKFurd0	item.comment	bn-bb1c855c4	{"body":"Groomed: expanded description with implementation pointer (detach handler already does tmux cleanup — shutdown should reuse that pattern), added acceptance criteria and testing strategy, added cli label"}	blake3:2PvqY9YnMvuyFu7lfi_SLkS0uXfmbvTzPEXZ0qYMZIU
1769363601092466	bob	itc:v3:AWKSc8kyZJPJk5EAAAAAQau9WtV610AAAAEzJw		item.create	bn-b505a2e82	{"description":"Interactive shells (bash) ignore SIGTERM, requiring users to remember -9. Change default to SIGKILL for reliable cleanup. Add --term flag for graceful SIGTERM when needed.\n\nImported beads fields:\nclose_reason:\nImplemented in commit defabd5\n\ncompaction_level:\n0\n\ncontent_hash:\n15e6e97608ec1794721a7529a40f8df5d60dbc155109380b29264717131b9bdd\n\nephemeral:\n0\n\nis_template:\n0\n\noriginal_size:\n0\n\npinned:\n0\n\nsource_repo:\n.","kind":"task","title":"Use SIGKILL as default for kill command"}	blake3:Va72-lRXmKprqneFdDg_pFkmh_qgzYKVbAX6rnVzdt0
1769363982756505	bob	itc:v3:AWKSc8kyZJPJk5EAAAAAQau9WtV610AAAAEzKA	blake3:Va72-lRXmKprqneFdDg_pFkmh_qgzYKVbAX6rnVzdt0	item.move	bn-b505a2e82	{"reason":"Imported from beads","state":"done"}	blake3:TW8GRapm69thMdkRGHe1n1ycNEfjQYozNaH_SAOxAFA
1769785212411365	bob	itc:v3:AWKSc8kyZJPJk5EAAAAAQau9WtV610AAAAEzKQ		item.create	bn-b9affcba9	{"description":"When running botty view, detaching, then running botty view again, agents can appear in a garbled state. This is accompanied by:\n\n  WARN botty::server: Attach session error: I/O error: Broken pipe (os error 32)\n\nRoot cause: botty view currently kills the existing tmux session and creates a fresh one every time. This tears down all the readonly attach connections (causing broken pipe errors) and re-establishes them, which can leave the screen in a garbled state during the transition.\n\nFix: botty view should check if a botty tmux session already exists. If it does, just reattach to it (tmux attach-session). Only create a new session if one doesn't exist. The event loop already handles adding/removing panes dynamically, so the existing session should stay up to date.\n\nImported beads fields:\nclose_reason:\nFixed: botty view now reattaches to existing tmux session instead of destroying/recreating. Added --new-session flag to force fresh session when needed.\n\ncompaction_level:\n0\n\ncontent_hash:\n2f0ce388f1da5cfa3525bbbcf9a6416df8095911ce76320fd571f1853ae27696\n\nephemeral:\n0\n\nis_template:\n0\n\noriginal_size:\n0\n\npinned:\n0\n\nsource_repo:\n.","kind":"bug","title":"botty view reattach: reuse existing tmux session instead of recreating"}	blake3:Gd_us-XPFnuuqZVeDeSPzxHXcZIE70SYxuX53axcXV8
1769786443238386	bob	itc:v3:AWKSc8kyZJPJk5EAAAAAQau9WtV610AAAAEzKg	blake3:Gd_us-XPFnuuqZVeDeSPzxHXcZIE70SYxuX53axcXV8	item.move	bn-b9affcba9	{"reason":"Imported from beads","state":"done"}	blake3:IguZ4kZavlTnzPi0ySYO7514jWtgC3AJ-S7dmRKlnQM
1769541218556509	bob	itc:v3:AWKSc8kyZJPJk5EAAAAAQau9WtV610AAAAEzKw		item.create	bn-b30ede978	{"description":"From security review cr-qmr8 (th-r7r3):\n\n## Original Report\n[MEDIUM] Protocol framing ambiguity. The code mixes JSON messages and raw binary PTY data on the same connection, relying on timing-based delimiters to distinguish them. This is fragile and could lead to protocol confusion attacks where PTY output is misinterpreted as control messages.\n\n## Current Decision: Won't Fix\n\nDeclined because:\n\n1. **Local IPC only** - There's no network attacker. The only parties are the client and server, both running as you.\n\n2. **Direction matters** - The \"confusion\" would be PTY output (from agent → client) being misinterpreted as server control messages. But PTY output flows in one direction after attach starts—there's no parsing of it as JSON.\n\n3. **In practice it works** - The initial JSON response is read before entering the raw I/O bridge. After that, everything is just PTY data forwarded to stdout.\n\n4. **Proper fix is expensive** - Length-prefixed framing or out-of-band signaling would require protocol changes, version negotiation, and client/server coordination. Overkill for a local tool.\n\n## If Revisited\nIf botty needs bidirectional control messages during attach (e.g., server-initiated disconnect, bandwidth throttling), proper framing would be needed. Options:\n- Length-prefixed binary framing (like HTTP/2)\n- Magic byte prefix for control messages (e.g., 0x00 + length + JSON)\n- Separate control socket\n\nImported beads fields:\nclose_reason:\nWon't fix: Protocol framing ambiguity is acceptable for local IPC tool. Documented in security review cr-qmr8. Would only revisit if botty needs remote connections or bidirectional control messages during attach.\n\ncompaction_level:\n0\n\ncontent_hash:\ncf50a9798c2d62d16d5dfd3e9031f9a655df8156b4c09c1fdbb2c2e82bf3b8fe\n\nephemeral:\n0\n\nis_template:\n0\n\noriginal_size:\n0\n\npinned:\n0\n\nsource_repo:\n.","kind":"task","title":"Consider explicit protocol framing for attach"}	blake3:L8LBRmFDKT4Af_4qHElh520x6XgZbP-s5_HZj2PHq94
1769874445612383	bob	itc:v3:AWKSc8kyZJPJk5EAAAAAQau9WtV610AAAAEzLA	blake3:L8LBRmFDKT4Af_4qHElh520x6XgZbP-s5_HZj2PHq94	item.move	bn-b30ede978	{"reason":"Imported from beads","state":"done"}	blake3:HXKIAzIA1k10wXVl8pNcj11lPkSRU8Vi5LiYBhi0-zo
1770654332132703	botty-dev	itc:v3:AWLnk5P-ZJJJxAAAAAAAQe9df9qquAAAAAEuCg		item.create	bn-bd1f6309d	{"description":"Update spawn, kill, send, snapshot, dump, recording, and gen-test to follow output conventions.\n\n## Commands to update\n- **spawn**: Output agent ID (text: just ID, json: `{ \"agent\": { \"id\": \"...\", \"pid\": N }, \"advice\": [\"botty send <id> ...\"] }`)\n- **kill/send**: Consistent success/error output with next-step advice\n- **snapshot**: Align format options (text/json/pretty instead of raw/jsonl)\n- **dump**: Align format options\n- **recording**: Already outputs JSON; add text format option\n- **doctor**: Already close; minor tweaks if needed\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] All mutation commands support --format text/json (pretty where it makes sense)\n- [ ] JSON responses always have advice[] field\n- [ ] Text output is ID-first with suggested next commands\n- [ ] No command uses bare println for structured output\n\n## Testing\n- Build and test each command\n- Verify JSON output with jq for all commands that support it\n\nImported beads fields:\nclose_reason:\nMerged. Spawn/kill/send/recording commands now support --format with text/json/pretty.\n\ncompaction_level:\n0\n\ncontent_hash:\na3010c4c5a70b172440df69259d5aef46242532609dce3cd0629bae3a3ecbcb2\n\nephemeral:\n0\n\nis_template:\n0\n\noriginal_size:\n0\n\nowner:\nbotty-dev\n\npinned:\n0\n\nsource_repo:\n.","kind":"task","title":"Update remaining commands to use OutputFormat conventions"}	blake3:VjpVQIJQ-04Sy-M81HtLzhjWOQq0lVU7_YnfyMi9duo
1770656138038763	botty-dev	itc:v3:AWLnk5P-ZJJJxAAAAAAAQe9df9qquAAAAAEuCw	blake3:VjpVQIJQ-04Sy-M81HtLzhjWOQq0lVU7_YnfyMi9duo	item.move	bn-bd1f6309d	{"reason":"Imported from beads","state":"done"}	blake3:NUalMsQRI-MiIzKZJ1mSNX7m3yOwoaI4swTH2zLG6Ic
1770393992915760	botty-dev	itc:v3:AWLnk5P-ZJJJxAAAAAAAQe9df9qquAAAAAEuDA		item.create	bn-b85190640	{"description":"Add a `signal` subcommand that sends arbitrary Unix signals to agent processes. Usage: `botty signal <agent> <signal>` where signal is a name (SIGUSR1, SIGHUP, SIGINT) or number. This is the low-level escape hatch; `kill` remains the high-level stop command. Supports --label, --all, --proc filters like kill does.\n\nImported beads fields:\nclose_reason:\nImplemented: botty signal <agent> --signal <SIG> sends arbitrary Unix signals. Supports names (TERM, USR1, HUP, etc.) and numbers. Case-insensitive, SIG prefix optional.\n\ncompaction_level:\n0\n\ncontent_hash:\nbb11f2e04b7d1f187e8e888112f0c1489de3747ef2ef45a3aa311c9fbb731169\n\nephemeral:\n0\n\nis_template:\n0\n\noriginal_size:\n0\n\nowner:\nbotty-dev\n\npinned:\n0\n\nsource_repo:\n.","kind":"task","title":"Add signal subcommand for sending arbitrary signals to agents"}	blake3:waRpvP6axe2ydnFLjQQunrg68YHP_DHf21BXcfM_Uw0
1770394813834462	botty-dev	itc:v3:AWLnk5P-ZJJJxAAAAAAAQe9df9qquAAAAAEuDQ	blake3:waRpvP6axe2ydnFLjQQunrg68YHP_DHf21BXcfM_Uw0	item.move	bn-b85190640	{"reason":"Imported from beads","state":"done"}	blake3:5OSvQNKNmwd26J4zqR2ZR9WEgTGTG9l-Xv7ya1lcWkM
1769541212703734	bob	itc:v3:AWKSc8kyZJPJk5EAAAAAQau9WtV610AAAAEzLQ		item.create	bn-b6e69bfa7	{"description":"From security review cr-qmr8 (th-bepr):\n\n## Original Report\n[CRITICAL] Unsafe signal sending to arbitrary PIDs. The server returns a PID which the client trusts and sends SIGWINCH to. A malicious or compromised server could return any PID, causing signals to be sent to unrelated processes. Additionally, PID reuse attacks are possible - if the original process dies and another process takes its PID, you'll signal the wrong process.\n\n## Current Decision: Won't Fix\n\nDeclined because:\n\n1. **Threat model mismatch** - botty is local IPC over a Unix socket. The server runs as the same user, on the same machine. If an attacker can compromise the server or MITM the socket, they already have code execution as your user—sending SIGWINCH to a process is the least of your problems.\n\n2. **We control the PID source** - The PID comes from our own spawn operation. The server tracks which PIDs it spawned. There's no external input.\n\n3. **SIGWINCH is benign** - Even if somehow the wrong process received it, SIGWINCH just tells a process \"your terminal resized.\" Most processes ignore it entirely. It can't cause privilege escalation or data corruption.\n\n4. **Fix would add complexity** - Moving signaling server-side means the server needs to track which attach clients want resize notifications, adding state and message types for minimal security benefit.\n\n## If Revisited\nIf botty ever supports remote connections or multi-user scenarios, this should be reconsidered. The fix would be to add a Request::SendSignal { agent_id, signal } that the server validates before forwarding.\n\nImported beads fields:\nclose_reason:\nWon't fix: SIGWINCH client-side signaling is acceptable for local tool with same-user threat model. Server tracks PIDs it spawned, SIGWINCH is benign. Documented in security review cr-qmr8. Would only revisit for remote/multi-user scenarios.\n\ncompaction_level:\n0\n\ncontent_hash:\n8cb714050fbb05c2bef912fdb21104c17efc9f81ba1ee8dee1a52c04f536020a\n\nephemeral:\n0\n\nis_template:\n0\n\noriginal_size:\n0\n\npinned:\n0\n\nsource_repo:\n.","kind":"task","title":"Consider moving SIGWINCH signaling server-side"}	blake3:JrSgY0_0578uz9yxAjJFzkIPo-7htnF9RGcPxUVvcXE
1769874447452753	bob	itc:v3:AWKSc8kyZJPJk5EAAAAAQau9WtV610AAAAEzLg	blake3:JrSgY0_0578uz9yxAjJFzkIPo-7htnF9RGcPxUVvcXE	item.move	bn-b6e69bfa7	{"reason":"Imported from beads","state":"done"}	blake3:SziooXVQ41myS_1NCxOH-zYURkVrn3Od4EYpjMu_kos
