1770581910734241	botty-dev	itc:v3:AWLnk5P-ZJJJxAAAAAAAQe9df9qquAAAAAEuEA		item.create	bn-b633f9ff9	{"description":"Allow `/` in agent names so agents spawning subagents can use a hierarchical naming convention like `parent/child`.\n\n## Current behavior\nAgent name validation (server/mod.rs:348) only allows `[a-zA-Z0-9_-]`. Slashes are rejected.\n\n## Proposed change\nAdd `/` to the allowed character set. Constraints:\n- No leading/trailing slashes\n- No double slashes (`//`)\n- Max one level of nesting may be sufficient (TBD)\n- Ensure slash does not cause issues with any path-based lookups or shell escaping\n\n## Convention\n```bash\n# Parent agent spawns children\nbotty spawn --name myagent/researcher -- ...\nbotty spawn --name myagent/implementer -- ...\n\n# List shows hierarchy\nbotty list  # myagent/researcher, myagent/implementer\n```\n\n## Consideration\nEvaluate whether slash needs special handling in any existing code paths (event routing, tmux pane naming, file paths, shell completion).\n\nImported beads fields:\nclose_reason:\nAlready released\n\ncompaction_level:\n0\n\ncontent_hash:\n8a8ae5b78b85ecdb4212ade36478ab99c7a3455043e3029f6899365d8b0970dc\n\nephemeral:\n0\n\nis_template:\n0\n\noriginal_size:\n0\n\nowner:\nbotty-dev\n\npinned:\n0\n\nsource_repo:\n.","kind":"task","title":"Allow slashes in agent names for parent/child convention"}	blake3:3gw3MaMsS5pxTBaC5Bjbs_6HRR3B1P8vtoVlALeItlM
1770643679682198	botty-dev	itc:v3:AWLnk5P-ZJJJxAAAAAAAQe9df9qquAAAAAEuEQ	blake3:3gw3MaMsS5pxTBaC5Bjbs_6HRR3B1P8vtoVlALeItlM	item.move	bn-b633f9ff9	{"reason":"Imported from beads","state":"done"}	blake3:LSYMM_QcKcUz-_O6_dQrVaHfSYUY8SyIDj_4Josgsuc
1769543521350993	bob	itc:v3:AWKSc8kyZJPJk5EAAAAAQau9WtV610AAAAEzQQ		item.create	bn-b664b2be8	{"description":"Currently the server shuts down when no PTYs are active, which kills the tmux session and kicks you out of botty view.\n\nDesired behavior:\n1. Run `botty view`\n2. Opens tmux session with 'waiting for agents...' placeholder\n3. Autonomous agent runs `botty spawn` → PTY appears in tmux\n4. PTY terminates → goes back to 'waiting for agents...'\n5. Repeat - view stays open as a persistent dashboard\n\nThis enables using botty view as a monitoring dashboard for agent orchestration, where agents spawn and terminate over time.\n\nImplementation considerations:\n- Server needs to stay alive when PTY count goes to zero\n- View mode needs a placeholder pane/message when no PTYs exist\n- May want different behavior for `view` (persistent) vs other commands (ephemeral)\n- Consider `--keep-alive` flag or make it default for view mode\n\nImported beads fields:\nclose_reason:\nImplemented in v0.3.0 - persistent view mode with waiting placeholder\n\ncompaction_level:\n0\n\ncontent_hash:\n910b7892d900c90621bb30aae5aa16482a87601fb6b84d13e9abaaed8bbbeca8\n\nephemeral:\n0\n\nis_template:\n0\n\noriginal_size:\n0\n\npinned:\n0\n\nsource_repo:\n.","kind":"task","title":"Keep server alive for persistent view mode"}	blake3:dpQ2_Ler6WVX3ASSfcKtmPUcwksE13TObzxWtWClE8o
1769560703554510	bob	itc:v3:AWKSc8kyZJPJk5EAAAAAQau9WtV610AAAAEzQg	blake3:dpQ2_Ler6WVX3ASSfcKtmPUcwksE13TObzxWtWClE8o	item.move	bn-b664b2be8	{"reason":"Imported from beads","state":"done"}	blake3:C7AopEaAR-pOG08xlMu-GIZRrRtW7bPPbncin5VwJX0
