1771273710614562	botty-dev	itc:v3:AWLnk5P-ZJJJxAAAAAAAQe9df9qquAAAAAEuFA		item.create	bn-b55b181c8	{"description":"The server handler for Request::Tail (src/server/mod.rs:569) ignores the lines parameter entirely (lines: _) and always returns agent.transcript.all_bytes(). The transcript has tail_bytes(n) but it works on byte count not line count. Need to: 1) convert lines to a byte-based tail (or add a tail_lines method to transcript), 2) use it in the server handler instead of all_bytes(). The follow-mode path in main.rs also uses Request::Tail but needs the full transcript for offset tracking, so lines should only limit the initial output in one-shot mode.\n\nImported beads fields:\nclose_reason:\nFixed in v0.13.1. Server now respects the lines parameter via new tail_lines() method. Follow mode passes lines=0 for full transcript offset tracking.\n\ncompaction_level:\n0\n\ncontent_hash:\nd3f5b4251f787342122b53c3bc4fba6e168fd63a949455529dba12f7acfb07b2\n\nephemeral:\n0\n\nis_template:\n0\n\noriginal_size:\n0\n\nowner:\nbotty-dev\n\npinned:\n0\n\nsource_repo:\n.","kind":"bug","title":"tail -n is ignored: server returns full transcript"}	blake3:ZgJwKLFNyUBQV1ByWteb30OqopmP04pCCTd3DPBeiYM
