1769712683222235	bob	itc:v3:AWKSc8kyZJPJk5EAAAAAQau9WtV610AAAAEzWw		item.create	bn-b107233b9	{"description":"Instead of hex codes like 'botty send-bytes id \"1b5b42\"' for arrow keys, support named sequences: 'botty send-key id down' or 'botty send id --key down'.\n\nCommon keys to support: up, down, left, right, enter, tab, escape, ctrl-c, ctrl-d, backspace, delete, home, end, pageup, pagedown.\n\nMakes test scripts much more readable. Fall back to hex for exotic sequences.\n\nExample:\nbotty send-key test-agent down\nbotty send-key test-agent enter\nbotty send-key test-agent ctrl-c\n\n## Triage Notes (2026-01-29)\n**Complexity**: Low-Medium - Extend parse_key_notation() (cli.rs:6-47) to return Vec<u8>, add ANSI sequence lookup table\n**Current**: Already handles ctrl-X, ^X, single chars for detach key\n**Implementation**: Create send-key subcommand or --key flag, reuse SendBytes protocol, ~2-4 hours\n**Value**: High - Common use case, dramatically improves test readability\n**Keep**: P2 (high value, low risk, isolated change)\n\nImported beads fields:\nclose_reason:\nImplemented in commit e231efe. Added 'botty send-key' command with support for arrow keys, special keys, navigation keys, control sequences, and function keys. Uses existing SendBytes protocol. Comprehensive tests added. All tests pass.\n\ncompaction_level:\n0\n\ncontent_hash:\n65ebbf13c76ac7403c6bf3c4637973c857137e0b8e674378bc6416340734c4e8\n\nephemeral:\n0\n\nis_template:\n0\n\noriginal_size:\n0\n\npinned:\n0\n\nsource_repo:\n.","kind":"task","title":"Add named key sequences to botty send"}	blake3:u185p02x5G3eD1mz8GB8YcKXW-AN-UcMR29WlfzrjKY
