1771184021337414	botty-dev	itc:v3:AWLnk5P-ZJJJxAAAAAAAQe9df9qquAAAAAEuFg		item.create	bn-bc365c495	{"description":"When the tmux session dies (e.g. killed externally, race on last pane), the event loop in run_view_event_loop (src/main.rs:2110) keeps processing queued events and spewing 'can't find session: botty' warnings for every add_pane/remove_pane call. Fix: detect session-not-found errors from tmux operations and break out of the event loop instead of continuing.\n\nImported beads fields:\nclose_reason:\nFixed in v0.13.0. Event loop checks session_exists() after tmux errors and breaks out.\n\ncompaction_level:\n0\n\ncontent_hash:\n944df1e34b05182090d6e9b2426e980f5254fdf5630b63ce610e9adb4db77f50\n\nephemeral:\n0\n\nis_template:\n0\n\noriginal_size:\n0\n\nowner:\nbotty-dev\n\npinned:\n0\n\nsource_repo:\n.","kind":"bug","title":"view event loop: bail out on dead tmux session"}	blake3:ybdAJ4DN23Oc5stUSwyqOwWjNk2VZ0vFD9khnpEmQ7Q
