1769544885530225	bob	itc:v3:AWKSc8kyZJPJk5EAAAAAQau9WtV610AAAAEzbQ		item.create	bn-ba91676d2	{"description":"When running botty view, the tmux resize hooks trigger in other tmux sessions too, showing error messages like:\n\n```\n'./target/release/botty resize-panes --mode=panes' returned 1\n'/home/bob/src/botty/target/release/botty resize-panes --mode=panes' returned 1\n```\n\nUser has to press 'q' to dismiss.\n\nThe hook is probably being set at the server level instead of just the botty session, or the resize-panes command is failing when called from outside the botty session context.\n\nShould either:\n1. Scope the hook to only the botty tmux session\n2. Make resize-panes fail silently when not in botty context\n3. Suppress tmux error display for the hook\n\nImported beads fields:\nclose_reason:\nFixed in commit c2e1904. Made resize-panes exit with code 0 even on errors (socket connection failures, etc). Since it's called from tmux hooks, failures are non-critical and we just log them as warnings instead of showing error popups to users. Tested and working.\n\ncompaction_level:\n0\n\ncontent_hash:\n44c82c7a9bcdb9672f396a9649b3475daace2dfe3a80a0c8129196cd4377af74\n\nephemeral:\n0\n\nis_template:\n0\n\noriginal_size:\n0\n\npinned:\n0\n\nsource_repo:\n.","kind":"bug","title":"Tmux resize hook errors shown in other sessions"}	blake3:ZFZuvmSSSHiEO2IMfgedvlcdwhROVx0eN5unmyMnxaE
