1770581900558460	botty-dev	itc:v3:AWLnk5P-ZJJJxAAAAAAAQe9df9qquAAAAAEuHQ		item.create	bn-b02985969	{"description":"Add --exited flag to `botty wait` that blocks until an agent exits, then returns the agent's exit code as the process exit code.\n\n## Use case\nAgents without subagent capabilities can use botty to spawn subagents, wait for them, then collect output:\n\n```bash\nbotty spawn --name sub1 -- do-thing-1\nbotty spawn --name sub2 -- do-thing-2\n\n# wait + collect (sequential)\nbotty wait --exited sub1 && botty dump sub1\nbotty wait --exited sub2 && botty dump sub2\n\n# or parallel\nbotty wait --exited sub1 & botty wait --exited sub2 & wait\nbotty dump sub1; botty dump sub2\n```\n\n## Behavior\n- If agent already exited: return immediately with its exit code\n- If agent is running: block until exit (subject to --timeout)\n- Exit code propagation: `botty wait --exited` exits with the agent's exit code\n- Composable with --print to dump final screen on exit\n- Show the above example in --help (after_help or long_about)\n\n## Implementation notes\n- Add `--exited` bool flag to the wait CLI args\n- Add server-side support: subscribe to events or poll agent state\n- The wait command already has timeout infrastructure to reuse\n\nImported beads fields:\nclose_reason:\nAlready released\n\ncompaction_level:\n0\n\ncontent_hash:\n018538c555ed7ab7f507a9d283b5add03fe60ac7c03d34ce40b689931d1e74c8\n\nephemeral:\n0\n\nis_template:\n0\n\noriginal_size:\n0\n\nowner:\nbotty-dev\n\npinned:\n0\n\nsource_repo:\n.","kind":"task","title":"Add --exited flag to botty wait"}	blake3:CRQTpN5A7UKy9A-dpJtWc-e865PIhS4v6Grv-LPKXE8
1770643678978013	botty-dev	itc:v3:AWLnk5P-ZJJJxAAAAAAAQe9df9qquAAAAAEuHg	blake3:CRQTpN5A7UKy9A-dpJtWc-e865PIhS4v6Grv-LPKXE8	item.move	bn-b02985969	{"reason":"Imported from beads","state":"done"}	blake3:ZEGf4Y0a8NqmEpSybixbYGA6ULRUTBLSDXDQnPUPuj4
