1770128639475063	bob	itc:v3:AWKSc8kyZJPJk5EAAAAAQau9WtV610AAAAEzsQE		item.create	bn-b093d75c9	{"description":"When all agents are closed/killed, the tmux pane title in `botty view` still shows the last agent's command (e.g., \"bash\" or \"htop\") instead of indicating no agents are running.\n\n## Expected behavior\nWhen no agents are running, the pane title should show \"Waiting for agents\" or similar idle indicator.\n\n## Reproduction\n1. `botty view`\n2. `botty spawn -- bash`\n3. `botty kill <agent-id>`\n4. Observe: pane title still shows \"bash\"\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] When all agents exit, pane title updates to an idle message (e.g., \"No agents\" or \"Waiting for agents\")\n- [ ] When a new agent spawns, pane title updates to show the new agent\n\n## Testing\n- Spawn an agent, kill it, verify pane title changes\n- Spawn multiple agents, kill all, verify title updates\n- Check with `tmux display -p \"#{pane_title}\"` in the botty session\n\nImported beads fields:\nclose_reason:\nMerged. Clears agent metadata from pane border when all agents exit.\n\ncompaction_level:\n0\n\ncontent_hash:\n897c51454c6478672da8e793e0c1335cdeae51747c24dca2c06dd2c6c97feeff\n\nephemeral:\n0\n\nis_template:\n0\n\noriginal_size:\n0\n\nowner:\nbotty-dev\n\npinned:\n0\n\nsource_repo:\n.","kind":"bug","title":"botty view tmux pane title shows previous agent command after all closed"}	blake3:X3s0zoknLJSL9fFVREhOFmUP1TlgFbPErfonmLsGNzw
